Commonly asked questions on Terraform in an Interview:

🧩 1️⃣ What is a Terraform State File?
The terraform.tfstate file is the source of truth for your infrastructure.
 It maps your Terraform configuration to real-world resources.
💡 Tip: Store it remotely (S3, Azure Blob, Terraform Cloud) for team collaboration and state locking.

🔒 2️⃣ What Happens If You Lose the State File?
 Terraform forgets what’s deployed — it might try to recreate everything! 😱
✅ Best Practice: Always use remote backends and enable versioning to recover easily.

⚙️ 3️⃣ What is Terraform Drift?
 Drift occurs when the actual infrastructure differs from what’s defined in your Terraform code.
🧠 Example: Someone changes an EC2 instance directly in the AWS Console.
 💬 Command to detect: terraform plan

🔁 4️⃣ How Do You Fix Drift?
 You can either:
🧩 Update your Terraform configuration to match actual changes, or
⚡ Run terraform apply to restore the desired state.

🌍 5️⃣ How to Handle Multiple Environments (Dev, Stage, Prod)?
 Use Workspaces or separate state files/backends for each environment.
 This keeps your infrastructure isolated, safe, and easy to manage.
